• 2 maker orders of amounts 400000 and 377000
• total amount = 400000 + 377000 = 777000
• Taker fee taken = 777000 * 100011 / 1000000 = 77708.547 = 77709 Maker fees would be 377000 * 100011 / 1000000 = 37704.147 = 37705 400000 * 100011 / 1000000 = 40004.4 = 40005 which is 1 wei more than actually taken. Below is a foundry test to reproduce the problem, which can be inserted into Claim.t.sol:
