Suspended bridge transactions cannot be restored. As a result, the assets will be stuck, and bridge service providers cannot reclaim the assets they have transferred to the users from the protocol. In Line 90 below, when restoring the bridge transaction, the invalid assets will be deposited into the account of bridgeLayout.invalidBridgedAmountsPool. These invalid assets can be withdrawn from this account/pool at a later time. Per Line 88 below, if the bridgeLayout.invalidBridgedAmountsPool is zero, the restoreBridgeTransaction transaction will revert. However, within the codebase, there is no way to update the bridgeLayout.invalidBridgedAmountsPool value. Thus, the bridgeLayout.invalidBridgedAmountsPool will always be zero. The restoreBridgeTransaction transaction will always revert and there is no way to restore a suspended bridge transaction. As a result, the assets will be stuck, and bridge service providers will not be able to reclaim the assets they have transferred to the users from the protocol. ocol-core/contracts/facets/Bridge/BridgeFacetImpl.sol#L88 File: BridgeFacetImpl.sol
