And lockAssets() pulls assets from the input "provider" address, transferring them to the vault. This means any user address who had asset token balance, and approved the vault contract (potential pending approvals from the past) is at risk of losing their funds here. The Manager can pull funds from a random provider address without any permissions, and the "provider" would lose his approved funds without getting anything in return.  

